  "description": "If you're reading this, surely you are aware of cyclocross:\n\na muddy, exhausting way to spend a Sunday morning. Should you be suffering\n\nfrom whatever it is that compels people to do 'cross, or merely lusting after\n\na truly versatile road/off-road bicycle, we present the Fuji Cross.\n\nThis is no hybrid or dirtified road bike. Produced in six sizes, Fuji's Cross\n\nis light, quick and race-ready, frame, wheels and parts. Components? What\n\nisn't (carefully selected) Shimano 105, Ritchey or Avid is Selle Italia, Zoom\n\nor Time. Frame and fork are Cro-Moly steel, cables appropriately routed. Race-ready. That said, as fine a 'cross tool as a Cross is, it's a\n\ngreat \"everything\" bike. A Cross won't complain if you don't race\n\nit.\n\nYou can ride trails and short road rides as-is. Or put skinny road tires on\n\nit; It'll roll like a road bike. Or mount fenders and lights on it and commute\n\nto work. Or put fat road tires on it, bolt a rack on it and it'll tour like\n\na... Well, not like a Fuji Tour, but darned well.\n\nGreat 'cross bike, great \"anything\" bike: Fuji Cross.",
